tr></tbody></table><table-wrap-foot><p>This table is a numerical expansion of figure 7 (systolic blood pressure). Estimates calculated using a two stage procedure in which the effect of drug treatment in reducing systolic blood pressure was first estimated,<sup>32</sup> then the effect of this blood pressure reduction on disease risk.<sup>25</sup></p><p>*See Methods (section headed &#x0201c;Predicting the trial results.&#x0201d;)</p></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap><table-wrap id="tbl4" position="float"><label>Table 4</label><caption><p>&#x02002;Estimates of preventive effect of taking one or more blood pressure lowering drugs on coronary heart disease (CHD) events and stroke according to pretreatment diastolic blood pressure, age, number of drugs, and dose (as multiple of standard<sup>33</sup>)</p></caption><table frame="hsides" rules="groups"><thead><tr><th colspan="1" rowspan="2" align="left" valign="bottom">Pretreatment diastolic blood pressure (mm Hg)</th><th colspan="1" rowspan="2" align="center" valign="bottom">Estimated reduction in diastolic blood pressure (mm Hg)</th><th colspan="5" rowspan="1" align="center" valign="bottom">Relative risk of CHD events by age (years)</th><th colspan="1" rowspan="2" align="center" valign="bottom"/><th colspan="5" rowspan="1" align="center" valign="bottom">Relative risk of stroke by age (years)</th></tr><tr><th colspan="1" rowspan="1" align="center" valign="bottom">40-49</th><th colspan="1" rowspan="1" align="center" valign="bottom">50-59</th><th colspan="1" rowspan="1" align="center" valign="bottom">60-69</th><th colspan="1" rowspan="1" align="center" valign="bottom">70-79</th><th colspan="1" rowspan="1" align="center" valign="bottom">80-89</th><th colspan="1" rowspan="1" align="center" valign="bottom">40-49</th><th colspan="1" rowspan="1" align="center" valign="bottom">50-59</th><th colspan="1" rowspan="1" align="center" valign="bottom">60-69</th><th colspan="1" rowspan="1" align="center" valign="bottom">70-79</th><th colspa